QU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"92cb9625c8930cd44fd4275b38d7b277ecdb0c94cd340b787576cec60ada75ba","event_uuid":"6894d6fc-a174-49bd-9549-e2c45731700a","position":{"commit_sha":"d57cfa5f791efb7edf636b2b0098b2799066aa4e","position":"1794531770073413145-6894d6fc-a174-49bd-9549-e2c45731700a"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"close_class":"preexisting","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Root cause, 2026-11-12 ~15:10 PST (read-only; figures kept in operator-local notes outside the repo; ratios only here).\nObservation:\n- The \"about 3x\" at 05:40 PST compared the cap's metered estimate with Cost Explorer's SAME-DAY figure. Re-read at 15:04 PST, Cost Explorer for 2026-11-12 had risen about 60%, and the ratio is now 1.94 (the metered value is frozen since the deny attached). Most of the 3x was Cost Explorer lag, not estimate error.\n- 2026-11-11, which Cost Explorer has fully settled (recomputing the day from per-ModelId token counts at the per-usage-type billed rates matches Cost Explorer within 1%), ran at 2.04, above the README's documented 1.1–1.9 band.\n- Cost Explorer's per-usage-type rates for the 5.5 models are lower than the 4.x rates the CEILING table was derived from (2026-09-25). For Opus 5.5 the ceiling is 1.56x the billed input, output and cache-write rates and 3.125x the billed cache-read rate; cache reads are about 90% of tokens on both days, and Opus 5.5 carries about 90% of the traffic.\nConclusion: the estimate is still an upper bound (correct direction) but runs about 2x for the 5.5 generation, because the ceilings remain tied to the 4.x price list (4.x models are still inside the 60-day derivation window) and cache reads dominate the token volume. The README band reflects the 4.x mix.\nFix options (operator decision, returned to the coordinator): (a) update the README band and its explanation only, keeping the accepted early-trip posture; (b) implement the README's own reserved remedy, an exact-match per-ModelId rate table that defaults to the ceiling (applied as a discount only for series that were read, so a missing read falls back to the ceiling), which would bring the 5.5 ratio near 1.25 but puts per-model unit rates in the public repo and lowers the safety margin.","timestamp":1794524744581832590},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Decision recorded 2026-11-12: land the README-only fix (option 1). Possible future story, deliberately NOT filed: an exact-match per-ModelId rate table defaulting to the ceiling (the README's reserved remedy), applied as a discount only for series actually read. Not taken here because it is a new mechanism and a bug fix may not add one; the ceilings still match their written definition and the README accepts early tripping.","timestamp":1794524882974749573},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Fixed in change 3385, merged as 5d519764f20 (LLM-Review +1, Verified +1; make verify rc=0). The README now states the 5.5-era band (about 1.8x Opus-only to 2.1x account-wide), the per-direction factors (about 1.56x; cache read about 3.1x), that cache reads drive the excess, and that comparisons must use settled days because Cost Explorer lags within the current UTC day (the ~3x sighting). Two new tests in tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py read CEILING from handler.py and pin the band to the dollar-weighted ratio (about 1.82) and the measured account-wide 2.04, ratios only; both failed RED on the old README. No price, threshold, attachment, handler or Terraform change. Possible future story (not filed): exact-match per-ModelId rate table.","timestamp":1794530825607923823},{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"HANDOFF STATE 2026-11-12 PST: CLOSED (class preexisting, completion signature signed). Change 3385 merged as 5d519764f20. Plan review and close ran through the worktree CLI on the Anthropic API. Worktree fix-oriole removed. Measured figures live only in operator-local notes outside the repo.","timestamp":1794531770073413145}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1794492037115943920,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"15b412a4-663e-41e1-9acb-68e4f354dc4c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1e1d-62cc-bb2f-46d1"}],"description":"## Observation (read-only, 2026-11-12 ~05:55 PST)\nThe spend-cap Lambda (`/aws/lambda/bedrock-spend-cap` log, ticks from 13:41Z onward) reported the metered (ceiling-priced CloudWatch token) estimate at about 3 times the Cost Explorer figure for the same UTC day, with `effective_source=metered`. The metered arm crossed the daily threshold and attached `BedrockDailySpendCapDeny` (about 05:40 PST), denying `bedrock:InvokeModel` to every capped role, including rebar-gerrit-instance-role, until the 00:00 UTC release.\n\ninfra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md documents the metered arm as an intentional upper bound, running at about 1.1 to 1.9 times settled billing. A ratio of about 3 is outside that band. Dollar figures are deliberately omitted (public tracker); they are in the Lambda log lines and Cost Explorer for 2026-11-12.\n\n## Root cause (measured; see comment)\nMost of the 3x was same-day Cost Explorer lag (re-read later, the 11-12 ratio is 1.94). The settled 2026-11-11 account-wide ratio is 2.04: the ceilings are tied to the 4.x price list, and for Opus 5.5 the cache-read ceiling is 3.125x the billed rate (other directions 1.5625x), with cache reads about 88% of Opus tokens. The ceilings still match their written definition; the documented band is stale.\n\n## Approach (decided 2026-11-12: README-only)\nUpdate `infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md`, ratios only:\n- Replace the 1.1-1.9x band with the measured band for the 5.5 generation, labelled by what each end is: about 1.8x for the Opus-only mix (lower end) to about 2.1x account-wide, where Sonnet traffic priced at the Opus ceilings raises it. State that cache reads drive the excess above 1.56x.\n- Explain that a same-day Cost Explorer comparison overstates the ratio because Cost Explorer lags intra-day (the \"about 3x\" sighting), so the comparison must use settled days.\nNo change to the handler, threshold, attachment, or Terraform. A per-model exact-match rate table remains a possible future story (not filed): it is a new mechanism, out of scope for a bug fix.\n\n## Testing\nExtend `tests/infra/test_bedrock_spend_cap_handler.py` (which already pins README content via `README_PATH`), ratios only, no new price data:\n- Read `CEILING` from `handler.py` with `ast` (already public). Encode only the Opus 5.5 ceiling-over-billed factors (1.5625 input/output/cache-write, 3.125 cache-read) and the 2026-11-11 Opus token-direction shares (input 0.0089, output 0.0194, cache read 0.8763, cache write 0.0954).\n- Compute ratio = Σ_d share_d·CEILING_d ÷ Σ_d share_d·(CEILING_d / factor_d), i.e. the factors weighted by each direction's billed-dollar share (about 1.82), and assert the README band's lower end is at or below it and its upper end at or above the measured account-wide 2.04, with the band inside [min factor, max factor].\n- Assert the README states the 1.56x and 3.1x factors, that cache reads drive the excess, and the same-day-lag / settled-day guidance.\nThese fail on the current README. `make verify` passes.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- [x] [non-codebase] The ratio for 2026-11-12 is re-measured against the SETTLED Cost Explorer day, and the cause of any excess over the documented band is identified from the per-direction token counts.\n  provenance: environment=AWS 896586841071 Cost Explorer and CloudWatch AWS/Bedrock (us-east-1); principal=frontier profile; privilege_posture=production-equivalent; instrument=live-call — ce get-cost-and-usage by service and usage type plus per-ModelId get-metric-data token sums for 2026-11-11 and 2026-11-12; ratios recorded in ticket comments, figures in operator-local notes\n- [x] Either the ceiling table is corrected or the README band is updated with the measured reason; no config key, env var or flag.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"infra/terraform/bedrock-spend-cap/README.md","reason":"measured band, cache-read note, settled-day comparison"},{"path":"tests/infra/test_bedrock_cap_readme_band.py","reason":"ratio-only pin of the README band"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","1e1d-62cc-bb2f-46d1"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"c0643697-b1b9-4587-9fea-a663c8cb6c62","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":[],"ticket_id":"b23c-8220-e09f-448a","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Bedrock spend-cap metered estimate ran about 3x settled billing on 2026-11-12, above the README's documented band","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["d8c5720c-9386-4998-af30-b812b22a7cfc","965e96ca-22df-41cf-be96-4ff4a2ce6449","a212f9b7-d059-4147-8833-aa2aeb6fa8a6","e2b8c2ac-eb81-43f3-ba38-26f4010128ff","ee62abb1-992d-4ba8-a237-51c99978499b","a0444fdc-16d1-497f-b761-5d13cee8e96a","e173d20b-3230-4a30-ab8a-adc29dcb4380","dba2f5c2-a1c5-4ef7-ae74-d2d15af5bef6","15b412a4-663e-41e1-9acb-68e4f354dc4c","1ce64f29-c3dd-4be4-88ba-96e8caf6228a","8a673139-1b02-4d2b-9c2d-61082750593f","badfa59f-e87d-4025-914b-20e97918ab83","c0643697-b1b9-4587-9fea-a663c8cb6c62","a39d5a0a-188a-4a2a-a0a8-c6d7f56f8036","6894d6fc-a174-49bd-9549-e2c45731700a"]},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1794531770073413146,"uuid":"135e0aad-821d-4c99-9dcd-722c24216412"}